            "output": "<path>/workspace/examples/creation_examples/example_ObsConditions.ipynb</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n10:     \"last run successfully: April 26, 2023\"\n11:    ]\n12:   },\n13:   {\n14:    \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n15:    \"id\": \"bad724e4\",\n16:    \"metadata\": {},\n17:    \"source\": [\n18:     \"The ObsCondition degrader can be used to generate spatially-varying photometric errors using input survey condition maps in `healpix` format, such as survey coadd depth, airmass, sky brightness etc. The photometric error is computed by `photerr.LsstErrorModel`, based on the LSST Overview Paper:\\n\",\n19:     \"https://arxiv.org/abs/0805.2366. \\n\",\n20:     \"\\n\",\n21:     \"The degrader assigns each object in the input catalogue with a pixel within the survey footprint and computes the magnitude error (SNR) on each pixel.\\n\",\n22:     \"The degrader takes the following arguments:\\n\",\n23:     \"\\n\",\n24:     \"- `nside`: nside used for the HEALPIX maps.\\n\",\n25:     \"- `mask`: Path to the mask covering the survey footprint in HEALPIX format. Notice that all negative values will be set to zero.\\n\",\n26:     \"- `weight`: Path to the weights HEALPIX format, used to assign sample galaxies in pixels. Default is weight=\\\"\\\", which uniform weighting.\\n\",\n27:     \"- `tot_nVis_flag`: If `nVisYr` is provided in `map_dict` (see below), this flag indicates whether the map shows the total number of visits in nYrObs (`tot_nVis_flag=True`), or the average number of visits per year (`tot_nVis_flag=False`). The default is set to `True`.   \\n\",\n28:     \"- `random_seed`: A random seed for reproducibility.\\n\",\n29:     \"- `map_dict`: A dictionary that contains the paths to the survey condition maps in HEALPIX format. This dictionary uses the same arguments as LSSTErrorModel. The following arguements, if supplied, may contain either a single number (as in the case of LSSTErrorModel), or a path to the corresponding survey condition map in `healpix` format:`m5`, `nVisYr`, `airmass`, `gamma`, `msky`, `theta`, `km`, and `tvis`. Notice that *except* `airmass` and `tvis`, for all other arguements, numbers/paths for *specific bands* should be passed. Other `LsstErrorModel` parameters can also be passed in this dictionary (e.g. a necessary one may be `nYrObs` for the survey condition maps; the default value is 10 years, although most  may be interested in early data releases). If any arguement is not passed, the default value in https://arxiv.org/abs/0805.2366 is adopted. Example:\\n\",\n30:     \"```json\\n\",\n31:     \"{\\n\",\n32:     \"   \\\"m5\\\": {\\\"u\\\": \\\"path\\\", ...}, \\n\",\n33:     \"   \\\"theta\\\": {\\\"u\\\": \\\"path\\\", ...},\\n\",\n34:     \"}\\n\",\n35:     \"```\\n\",\n36:     \"\\n\",\n37:     \"Argument defaults are determined by the defaults of the `LsstErrorModel` in [PhotErr](https://github.com/jfcrenshaw/photerr).\"\n38:    ]\n39:   },\n\n(Showing lines 10-39 of 447. Use offset=40 to continue.)\n</content>",
            "metadata": {
              "preview": "    \"last run successfully: April 26, 2023\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n   \"id\": \"bad724e4\",\n   \"metadata\": {},\n   \"source\": [\n    \"The ObsCondition degrader can be used to generate spatially-varying photometric errors using input survey condition maps in `healpix` format, such as survey coadd depth, airmass, sky brightness etc. The photometric error is computed by `photerr.LsstErrorModel`, based on the LSST Overview Paper:\\n\",\n    \"https://arxiv.org/abs/0805.2366. \\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"The degrader assigns each object in the input catalogue with a pixel within the survey footprint and computes the magnitude error (SNR) on each pixel.\\n\",\n    \"The degrader takes the following arguments:\\n\",\n    \"\\n\",\n    \"- `nside`: nside used for the HEALPIX maps.\\n\",\n    \"- `mask`: Path to the mask covering the survey footprint in HEALPIX format. Notice that all negative values will be set to zero.\\n\",\n    \"- `weight`: Path to the weights HEALPIX format, used to assign sample galaxies in pixels. Default is weight=\\\"\\\", which uniform weighting.\\n\",\n    \"- `tot_nVis_flag`: If `nVisYr` is provided in `map_dict` (see below), this flag indicates whether the map shows the total number of visits in nYrObs (`tot_nVis_flag=True`), or the average number of visits per year (`tot_nVis_flag=False`). The default is set to `True`.   \\n\",\n    \"- `random_seed`: A random seed for reproducibility.\\n\",\n    \"- `map_dict`: A dictionary that contains the paths to the survey condition maps in HEALPIX format. This dictionary uses the same arguments as LSSTErrorModel. The following arguements, if supplied, may contain either a single number (as in the case of LSSTErrorModel), or a path to the corresponding survey condition map in `healpix` format:`m5`, `nVisYr`, `airmass`, `gamma`, `msky`, `theta`, `km`, and `tvis`. Notice that *except* `airmass` and `tvis`, for all other arguements, numbers/paths for *specific bands* should be passed. Other `LsstErrorModel` parameters can also be passed in this dictionary (e.g. a necessary one may be `nYrObs` for the survey condition maps; the default value is 10 years, although most  may be interested in early data releases). If any arguement is not passed, the default value in https://arxiv.org/abs/0805.2366 is adopted. Example:\\n\",",
              "truncated": true,
